# Tables: Row header marks the cell that names its row, read by a screen reader with each cell of the row.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Tables · Row header
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For element: Cell
			Box:
				Border: 0 0 0.5 0
				Border color: rule
		For element: Header cell
			Typography:
				Bold: true
		For style: time
			Typography:
				Bold: true
				Color: accent
	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Row header
		Paragraph: The cells of `Header rows` are column headers. `Row header: true` makes a body cell the header of its row: in the tagged PDF a screen reader announces it with each cell of the row. It does not change the look, so the times here take a style as well.
			Style: intro
		Table:
			Column sizes: 70 * * *
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Time
					Cell: Monday
					Cell: Wednesday
					Cell: Friday
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Cell: 09:00
						Row header: true
						Style: time
					Cell: Mathematics
					Cell: History
					Cell: Mathematics
				Row:
					Cell: 10:00
						Row header: true
						Style: time
					Cell: Biology
					Cell: Mathematics
					Cell: Physics
				Row:
					Cell: 11:30
						Row header: true
						Style: time
					Cell: English
					Cell: Physics
					Cell: Music
